{"name":"Décor White","hex":"#f2e5cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"décor","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of decor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/d%C3%A9cor"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Interior design","blocks":[{"text":"Interior design is the art and science of enhancing the interior of a building to achieve a healthier and more aesthetically pleasing environment for the people using the space. With a keen eye for detail and a creative flair, an interior designer is someone who plans, researches, coordinates, and manages such enhancement projects. Interior design is a multifaceted profession that includes conceptual development, space planning, site inspections, programming, research, communicating with the stakeholders of a project, construction management, and execution of the design. Interior designers make use of fundamental design principles from the visual arts used to help viewers understand a given scene."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/30th_Street_Station_concourse_looking_west_July_2026.jpeg/330px-30th_Street_Station_concourse_looking_west_July_2026.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interior_design"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Lobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG/500px-Lobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Lobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG/1280px-Lobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Lobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG/500px-Lobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The lobby of Hotel Bristol, Warsaw","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALobby_Hotel_Bristol_w_Warszawie.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Balliol_College_Dining_Hall%2C_Oxford_-_Diliff.jpg/500px-Balliol_College_Dining_Hall%2C_Oxford_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Balliol_College_Dining_Hall%2C_Oxford_-_Diliff.jpg/1280px-Balliol_College_Dining_Hall%2C_Oxford_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Balliol_College_Dining_Hall%2C_Oxford_-_Diliff.jpg/500px-Balliol_College_Dining_Hall%2C_Oxford_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u